  "name": "IMMUNOGLOBULIN PROFILE SERUM",
  "code": "1121",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"187\" data-end=\"529\">The serum immunoglobulin profile measures the levels of the major classes of immunoglobulins: IgG, IgA, and IgM. These antibodies are critical components of the humoral immune system and are produced in response to infections, immune stimuli, or underlying disorders. This test is primarily used to:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"530\" data-end=\"789\">\n<li data-start=\"530\" data-end=\"556\">\n<p data-start=\"532\" data-end=\"556\">Assess immune function</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"557\" data-end=\"622\">\n<p data-start=\"559\" data-end=\"622\">Detect immunodeficiencies or excess immunoglobulin production</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"623\" data-end=\"728\">\n<p data-start=\"625\" data-end=\"728\">Evaluate chronic infections, autoimmune diseases, and plasma cell dyscrasias (e.g., multiple myeloma)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"729\" data-end=\"789\">\n<p data-start=\"731\" data-end=\"789\">Monitor response to treatment in immune-related conditions</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Immunoglobulin</th>\n<th>Elevated Levels May Indicate</th>\n<th>Decreased Levels May Indicate</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>IgG</strong></td>\n<td>Chronic infections, autoimmune diseases (e.g., lupus, rheumatoid arthritis), liver disease, multiple myeloma</td>\n<td>Primary or secondary immunodeficiency (e.g., CVID), nephrotic syndrome, protein-losing enteropathy</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>IgA</strong></td>\n<td>Chronic liver disease, chronic mucosal infections, autoimmune diseases, IgA myeloma</td>\n<td>Selective IgA deficiency, congenital immunodeficiencies, nephrotic syndrome</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>IgM</strong></td>\n<td>Acute infections, autoimmune diseases, Waldenstr&ouml;m&rsquo;s macroglobulinemia, chronic liver disease</td>\n<td>Selective IgM deficiency, certain leukemias/lymphomas, immunosuppressive therapy</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
